mem:constraint-01m7qrnss9twhf6mb2a7tebppq a mem:Constraint ;
    mem:content "Agents collaborating on Habitat hide nothing from each other. A file, source or locator left out of a packet or message is noise reduction, not confidentiality: do not turn an omission into a read ban or a leakage finding, and name files, paths and sources when that makes a message clearer. Isolation applies only as experiment design to the specific fresh evaluator or scorer of a held-out test, which must not see the held-out answers. Credentials never go in messages." ;
    mem:tag "agent-bus" ;
    mem:tag "agents" ;
    mem:tag "collaboration" ;
    mem:tag "evaluation" ;
    mem:tag "held-out" ;
    mem:tag "openness" ;
    mem:tag "references" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:severity "should" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T16:43:40.201017+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Owner correction after an agent treated a file omitted from a review copy as confidential and banned collaborators from reading it." .

mem:decision-01m7qrnstmn6wwwvr0tc64dzp2 a mem:Decision ;
    mem:content "Habitat recovery coordination: the Codex recovery director integrates priorities and decisions; the Claude director owns Claude staffing and independent challenge; the owner keeps product intent and admission of repairs and releases. Each working lane pairs a Codex lead with a Claude lead, one owning the artifact and the other challenging it. On the agent bus, directory habitat routes it: topic habitat carries director decisions only, and each lane works in its own concern topic. A second runtime agreeing is not an independent verdict." ;
    mem:tag "agent-bus" ;
    mem:tag "claude" ;
    mem:tag "codex" ;
    mem:tag "coordination" ;
    mem:tag "directors" ;
    mem:tag "leads" ;
    mem:tag "recovery" ;
    mem:tag "staffing" ;
    mem:scope mem:repo ;
    mem:artifactRef "docs/projects/habitat-sdk-recovery/triage.md" ;
    mem:branch "main" ;
    mem:createdAt "2026-11-18T16:43:40.244600+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    mem:rationale "Two runtimes work the recovery; one integrator avoids split direction while a separate staffing owner keeps independent challenge." ;
    mem:alternatives "single director for both runtimes,per-lane directors with no integrator" .
